someone wrote (hilarious PC 3.0.10 bug:)
>>It seems that every so often the save file gets corrupted for some reason, 
>>and when I restore the game, I find myself equipped with a +5 potion of 
>>cookies, a blessed +1 ., and a cloak of apples.

frog@gpu.utcs.utoronto.ca (F. Thinh-Ball) adds:
>With regard to copying saved files, DON'T put saved games on your 
>hard drive and COMPRESS disk thereafter! The same junk will result!

Knowledgeable people, please confirm/deny this rumour.

This certainly wasn't true in PC Nethack 3.0.5. I still haven't installed
a newer version (no, it's not really because of polymorphing tools, wands, etc)
and hesitate to do so if this is true now.

If frog means "encrypt" by "COMPRESS", I'd understand it :-).
If he really means "optimize the way stuff is stored on hard disk by
putting files all in one place and eliminating gaps, without changing
the actual data",
then it would be absolutely ludicrous if this were true.
I keep some save files (e.g. of visiting friends) around for very long
times. I also regularly compress my harddisk. The compression program says
that only certain memory-resident programs will be affected.
(On my PC, nethack is only memory-resident from a couple of minutes
after I turn it on until just before I turn it off again :-)

